In article <walker.740931598@mits> walker@mits.mdata.fi (Jukka Lahtinen)
dispenses some incorrect information:
>visentin@mundil.cs.mu.OZ.AU (Michael Alfred VISENTIN) writes:
>>1. What do you do with statues and figurines ??
>
>If you break a statue with a pick-axe or a wand of striking/digging, you
>MIGHT find a spellbook. If you apply a figurine, you get a pet.

	That's not entirely true.  Statues can be smashed with a pick-axe, a
wand of striking, or a spell of force bolt.  A wand of digging won't work.
Applying a cursed figurine will create a hostile creature, not a pet, so
ensure the figurine is not cursed before applying it (more on that below).

>>2. Is it OK to eat a unicorn corpse?
>
>Yes, if it is not your own alignment. (white for lawful, gray for neutral,
>black for chaotic)

	Even if it is of your own alignment, you still won't suffer for it.
You are penalized for killing a co-aligned unicorn, not for eating it.

>>3. Does anyone have any general strategies/philosophies for playing 
>>   the game e.g. do you do the Gnomish mines ASAP, or go to down to 
>>   dungeon level 10 and then do them; is it best to quaff every 
>>   potion and read every scroll you get etc...

	I usually enter the mines at my first opportunity.  As for items, I
always wait to use them until I am sure they are not cursed.  You can tell
whether an item is cursed or not by dropping it onto an altar or getting your
pet to step on it.  Your pet will go out of its way not to step on a cursed
item.  There are three scrolls you must watch for:  amnesia, fire, and destroy
armor.  I don't read any spellbooks until I've read a scroll of amnesia, I
always drop everything flammable (?!+) and step away before reading a scroll
that might be fire, and I always remove all but one unimportant piece of armor
before reading a scroll that might be destroy armor.  That's the way I do it,
anyway.

